# Stitch TaskbarBuddy

A small Electron desktop pet. A Stitch character sits quietly in the corner of your screen, right above the taskbar, and plays through animations throughout the day. Made as a personal gift.

## Features

- Sits in the corner of the screen, always on top
- Idle animation loop
- Multiple animations (idle, jump, fall, hurt, sleepy), right-click/click to switch
- Automatically switches to a "sleepy" animation late at night
- Launches automatically on login
- Stays visible even in fullscreen apps

## Tech stack

- [Electron](https://www.electronjs.org/) : cross-platform desktop app framework
- HTML5 Canvas for sprite animation
- Packaged with `electron-packager`

## Running locally

- bash
npm install
npx electron .


## Building

- bash
npx electron-packager . stitch-TaskbarBuddy --platform=darwin --arch=arm64 --out=dist

(Swap arm64 for x64 or universal depending on target Mac hardware.)

## Notes

Built as a first Electron project, a learning experience in desktop app windows, canvas animation, and Mac app packaging/permissions quirks.